## Flow Blocks

::: accordion {style=outline}
:: Identification
Document what happened, where, and who is exposed.

:: Assessment
Estimate severity and likelihood.

:: Control
Apply elimination, substitution, engineering, then admin/PPE.
:::

::: tabs
:: Before Shift
Check unresolved items from prior shift.

:: During Shift
Capture new hazards quickly.

:: After Shift
Confirm all incidents are documented.
:::

::: columns
::
### Hazards

- Chemical
- Electrical
- Ergonomic

::
### Controls

- Ventilation
- Lockout/tagout
- Lift assist
:::

::: sequence {style=numbered}
:: Step 1
Identify the issue.

:: Step 2
Assess risk.

:: Step 3
Apply controls.
:::

::: comparison {layout=side-by-side}
:: Before
Manual forms with delayed escalation.

:: After
Real-time logging and notifications.
:::

::: cards Scenario Card
:: Scenario Card {level=3}
A pressure alarm triggers during startup. Review context and choose a response.
:::

::: cards What is lockout/tagout?
:: What is lockout/tagout? {level=3}
Energy isolation before maintenance.

::: back
A lockout/tagout procedure isolates hazardous energy before maintenance starts.
:::
:::

# Final Checkpoint {hideTitle}

::: group Final Checkpoint {mode=all showResultsSummary passingScore=75}
::: choice Which action is safest first? {points=2 required shuffle}
( ) Keep operating and monitor
(x) Stop work and isolate hazard
( ) Ask for review after completion
:::
::: choice Select all valid controls {points=3 shuffle}
[x] Guard rail
[x] Ventilation
[ ] Ignore warning alarm
[x] PPE for residual risk
:::
::: match Match hazard to control {points=3 shuffle}
- Slip risk -> Housekeeping
- Electrical fault -> Lockout/tagout
- Noise exposure -> Hearing protection
:::
::: order Put response steps in order {points=3 shuffle}
1. Stop work
2. Secure area
3. Notify lead
4. Record incident
:::
::: free-response Describe one prevention strategy {points=5 required}
placeholder: Focus on one engineering control and one communication process.
:::
::: fill-blank Complete the sentence {points=2}
Before restart, verify {isolation} and confirm {authorization}.
:::
::: hotspot Select the pull pin. {points=4}
![Fire extinguisher diagram](/assets/extinguisher-diagram.png)
- Gauge {x=28 y=18}
- Pull pin {x=42 y=25 correct}
- Nozzle {x=65 y=39}
:::
::: rating Confidence with emergency protocol {required}
1. Not confident
2. Somewhat confident
3. Confident
4. Very confident
5. Expert
:::
::: categorize Sort controls by category {points=4 shuffle}
:: Engineering Controls
- Guard rail
- Ventilation
:: Administrative Controls
- Shift checklist
- Permit workflow
:::
:::

# Interactive Blocks {hideTitle}

## Interactive Blocks

::: checklist {required}
- [ ] Confirm route maps are posted
- [ ] Verify alarms are audible
- [ ] Review first-aid inventory
:::

::: signature I confirm this module was reviewed {mode=type}
:::

